In article <1992Feb13.014448.20758@wdl1.wdl.loral.com> dcb@wdl1.wdl.loral.com (David C Blume) writes:
>My question is:  If you get a wish EARLY in the game -- when you're in
>need of good armor AND weapons- would you wish for the weapon or the armor?
>
>The FAQ is: What are the best things to wish for?
>And I think it and its answer should be in the FAQ.  Perhaps only after a ^L.
>

When this (rarely) happens to me, I always go for that blessed +3 broadsword
named Stormbringer.  Dragon scale mail is good, I admit, but by the time
you reach Dlvl ~7, most monsters won't have a great deal of trouble hitting
you.  I prefer something that I probably won't see during the game.
If one has a kick-ass weapon, the armor will usually follow.
On thinking about it, I would get blessed +3 boots of speed before dragon
scale mail but after Stormy.  These are great to have, especially if
you have to run away.  They also protect from those nasty xans (xan? What
is the plural of xan?).  Blessed potions of invisibility are nice, but
relatively simple to get.  They would be further down on the old wish
list.  A bag of holding is nice as well, comes in after speed boots but
before bl. potion invis.


